     "explanation": "Emerging individual interest is the pivotal third phase where engagement stops depending on outside prompting and the person begins to voluntarily return to the activity and build genuine knowledge. Triggered and maintained situational interest (phases one and two) still rely on external sparks or support, while well-developed individual interest (phase four) is the mature, self-sustaining endpoint that comes after emergence, not the turning point itself.",
