     "explanation": "Self-report scales lose accuracy under high-stakes conditions because applicants can learn to answer strategically, and using a personality scale as a hard hiring gate raises real legal and fairness concerns. The far more defensible use of this research is organizational: since attrition concentrates in a predictable early window, employers should build feedback, mentorship, and stretch goals into that window rather than trying to screen it out with a single questionnaire.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"34\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"140\" width=\"860\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">USING GRIT RESEARCH RESPONSIBLY</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grit predicts retention well in research settings -</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">but a mandatory hiring gate invites faking and risk.</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"400\" width=\"860\" height=\"560\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The better use: design supportive first-90-day</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">environments around the exact window where most</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">attrition concentrates, rather than screening for it.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Weighing the responsible versus irresponsible uses of workplace grit research."
     }
