     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Hard Thing Rule and the Five-Component Framework",
     "content": "Duckworth's own family used what she calls the Hard Thing Rule to build grit deliberately rather than hope it would appear on its own. It has three parts. Everyone in the family, parents included, must be doing one hard thing that requires daily deliberate practice. You are allowed to quit, but only at a natural stopping point - a season's end, a program's completion, a contract's expiration - never in the middle of a bad week. And you get to choose your own hard thing; nobody else picks it for you, because passion has to attach to something you actually chose.\n\nThis capstone maps five components from the deeper lessons onto that same structure. Measurement means taking an honest baseline reading of your passion and perseverance, understood as a rough instrument rather than a verdict. Deliberate practice means designing weekly, feedback-rich blocks around your hard thing's specific weak points. Interest cultivation means committing to enough repeated exposures for the activity to move past a fragile initial spark. Hope means having a ready script for the setback that will inevitably arrive partway through. Environment means deliberately choosing the mentors, community, or team that will supply the outside support no single person sustains alone. Together these five components turn the Hard Thing Rule from a slogan into an operating system.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Hard Thing Rule</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Three parts, one operating system</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Three Parts</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Everyone does a hard</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"337\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thing with daily practice</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"374\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Quit only at a natural</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"411\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stopping point</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. You pick your own</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">hard thing</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(14,165,233,0.15)\" stroke=\"#0ea5e9\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Five Mapped Components</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Measurement, deliberate</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"337\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">practice, interest</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"374\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cultivation, hope, and</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"411\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">supportive environment</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"1000\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">From Slogan to Operating System</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"715\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Hard Thing Rule sets the container - one goal, a real quitting rule, your own choice.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"754\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The five components are what actually run inside that container week after week.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Duckworth's family rule, mapped onto the five deeper components from this course."
     }
