     "type": "application",
     "title": "Write Your One-Page Grit Development Plan",
     "content": "Use this final worksheet to build your own plan today, in the same structure Maria's example followed. Write real answers, not placeholders - the plan only works if it is genuinely yours.\n\n1. Name your hard thing and, in one sentence, why it matters to you right now.\n\n2. Take the Grit Scale today as your honest baseline, write today's date, and calendar a retest in six months.\n\n3. Design one weekly deliberate-practice block with a named feedback source - a coach, a recording, a mentor, or a measurable metric.\n\n4. Commit in writing to a minimum number of sessions, at least six to eight, before you allow yourself to judge whether this activity truly fits.\n\n5. Write your twenty-four-hour setback script in advance, before you need it, so a bad week does not become the moment you quietly disappear.\n\n6. Name one mentor, community, or team that will supply outside support, since no single person sustains grit entirely alone.\n\n7. Write your natural stopping point in advance - the specific date or milestone at which you are allowed to reconsider, and not one day before it.",
